## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: state=newGame() single object; rand(S) mulberry32 uses S.rngState; beginTurn/finishTurn call stormResolve→drawEvent→production→needs→fatigueSkill→migration→tradeTick→tickTimers in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: W=8,H=8,NT=64; genMap uses rand(S) seeded; tryBuild checks B.terr.includes(t.terr); adjInfo mult feeds into production() mult. Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: forge ore+power→metal, workshop metal+power→parts, greenhouse soil+water→food; applyCaps() enforces caps and logs overflow. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: colonist records {skill,fatigue,morale,job,at}; skillMult/fatigueMult/moraleMult read c.skill/fatigue/morale inside production(). Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: needs() consumes food/water, −12/−8 morale on shortage; moraleMult(c) used in production; fed&wat gives +3 morale recovery, not instant death. Score 2.

**F6 Research**: RESEARCH has 10 nodes; tryResearch enforces req[] and deducts cost; researchMult() and hasR() checks apply real effects in production/storm/trade. Score 2.

**F7 Events**: EVENTS array has 12 entries; weighted roll in drawEvent(); 5 events (wanderers, cache, fever, preacher, deserter) have differing choice effects; eventCds enforce EVENT_CD cooldown. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: priceOf() uses stockpile scarcity + T.drift; T.stock decremented on buy, incremented on sell; both doBuy/doSell implemented. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: stormResolve fires via stormNext; stormSeverity(turn) grows with turn/12; t.dis buildings skipped in production (zero output); forecast/reinforce research reduce dmg; tryRepair spends parts. Score 2.

**F10 Save/load**: serialize(S)→textarea; tryLoad parses+validateState() shows error via savemsg. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: win via S.turn===60 && winFlag check; lose via colonists.length===0→S.dead; calcScore uses pop/research/stock/turn/win; showSummary renders table. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: UI.tab switching via render(); log lines prefixed T+l.t; extensive data-tip tooltips; Space/1-6 keydown handlers; @media(max-width:420px) rule. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: runTests() checks negative res, cap overflow, roster consistency, morale bounds, save/load hash match — real invariants; runBenchmark/stepHeadless runs 200 turns headless, prints stateHash. Score 2.

**G1**: researchMult(S,key) reads hasR() flags, multiplies into production() mult every turn, shown in tile report. Score 4.

**G2**: needs() lowers c.morale on shortage; moraleMult(c) consumed in production() mult calc next turn. Score 4.

**G3**: stormResolve reduces t.hp, sets t.dis at 0hp; production() only zeroes output when t.dis (partial damage still full output); tryRepair spends parts+fatigue, restores hp/dis. Gap: non-knockout damage doesn't reduce yield. Score 2.

**G4**: priceOf() = TRADE_BASE×T.drift[g](drifts via tradeTick)×scarcity(S.res[g]/capFor); read in buyPrice/sellPrice/doBuy/doSell. Score 4.

**G5**: wanderers/cache/fever choice branches mutate S.res, S.colonists, c.fatigue, morale differently per branch, not just log. Score 4.

